# ===========================================================================
# Root .gitignore — covers backend/, frontend/, and repo-wide files
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / Editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment & secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
certs/*.crt
certs/*.key
certs/*.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docker-compose.override.yml
postgres_data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backups
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backups/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seed data — operator-specific, never part of the codebase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seeding is external to the application (see docs/explanation/architecture.md). A seeds/
# directory holds one operator's real personnel, projects and assignments, so this is a guard
# rather than a convenience: the rule used to live only in prose, and prose does not stop
# `git add -A`.
seeds/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kiro / IDE config (optional — remove if you want these tracked)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.kiro
.vscode

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (backend/)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
*.db
test.db
.coverage
coverage/

# Ruff
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node.js / TypeScript (frontend/)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# Incremental build state. This project type-checks with `tsc -b`, which writes a .tsbuildinfo per
# referenced project. Committing one poisons every other clone: the build trusts it and can report
# clean while the code does not compile.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Logs
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# code2prompt output. Regenerable, so it is never committed — but the reason it is listed here is
# sharper than tidiness: an output file left in the tree gets swallowed by the NEXT run. A dump of
# this repository measured 1.82 million tokens, and 911K of that — half — was a previous repo.md
# reading itself. The ignore rule is what stops that from compounding.
#
# .context/ holds the chunked dumps produced by scripts/context_chunks.py, regenerated on a schedule.
# The script excludes the directory from its own input for the same reason.
.context/
repo.md
repo-structure.md
code2prompt-*.md
*.c2p.md

# MkDocs build output. Not ignored until now, which made a local `mkdocs build --strict` leave an
# untracked directory that `git add -A` would happily commit — several hundred generated files.
# CI builds and publishes it; nobody needs it in the tree.
/site/
